  Check migrations for statements that lock tables, rewrite
  them or break running code.

  With no arguments, migrail finds the migrations in the
  repository and detects the migration tool. Pass migration
  files or directories to check only those, or - to read SQL
  from standard input.

  [1;34mUsage[m
    migrail check [path]... | - [flags]

  [1;34mFlags[m
        [1m--ci[m                  CI mode: no color,
                              links or spinners
                              unless forced
        [1m--compact[m             print one line per finding
        [1m--db-version string[m   PostgreSQL major
                              version in production,
                              such as 16 (default: 12)
    [1m-d, --dir string[m          project root to search
                              for migrations
                              (default: the
                              repository root)
        [1m--fail-on string[m      exit with code 1 on
                              findings at or above:
                              error, warning, notice
                              or never (default "error")
    [1m-f, --format string[m       output format: pretty
                              or json (default "pretty")
        [1m--framework string[m    migration tool to use
                              instead of detecting
                              it: sqitch, atlas,
                              prisma, drizzle,
                              goose, dbmate,
                              golang-migrate, flyway, sql
    [1m-q, --quiet[m               print only findings
                              and the summary
    [1m-r, --rule strings[m        only run these rules,
                              by ID or slug
        [1m--skip-rule strings[m   skip these rules, by
                              ID or slug
    [1m-v, --verbose[m             print each phase with
                              its timing

  [1;34mGlobal flags[m
        [1m--ascii[m           use ASCII symbols instead
                          of Unicode
        [1m--color string[m    use color: auto, always or
                          never (default "auto")
        [1m--no-hyperlinks[m   don't print clickable file
                          links
        [1m--theme string[m    color theme: auto, dark,
                          light or mono (default "auto")
